  "verdict": "Verdict (precision-first, vs best simple baseline TF-IDF+SVC): RoBERTa is below the best simple baseline by 1.30 precision points on the text test set (RoBERTa 0.9690 vs SVC 0.9820; McNemar p = 0.2530) at 28.6x CPU latency and 31.4x parameters. GPU latency multiple: NOT MEASURED (TF-IDF has no GPU implementation). Its complexity is NOT justified by a precision gain on this dataset. BiLSTM is also below SVC, by 1.00 precision points (0.9719 vs 0.9820; paired seed-42 McNemar p = 3.64e-08 \u2014 SVC is significantly better than BiLSTM on test errors), at 2.35x CPU latency and 1.57x parameters. In plain terms: on this old, highly separable Enron-style test set the cheapest model wins on precision, and neither neural model earns its cost in accuracy \u2014 RoBERTa does buy the highest recall (0.9932 vs SVC 0.9889) and the LITA explanations plus image/PDF/QR handling the baselines do not provide, while BiLSTM buys the fastest explanations (1.87 s/email vs RoBERTa 30.87 s/email). Whether that is worth it depends on the deployment budget, not on accuracy.",
